  "fits": [
    {
      "fact": "The 30B suits nano and small tanks, up to about 18 inches (45 cm).",
      "source": 9
    },
    {
      "fact": "The B line is made for plants that need low to medium light, such as Anubias, Java fern and mosses.",
      "source": 7
    },
    {
      "fact": "It works well for low-tech planted tanks and freshwater tanks with fish only.",
      "source": 8
    },
    {
      "fact": "A Vietnamese shop recommends it for shrimp- or snail-only tanks, or for undemanding plants such as ferns, moss and Bucephalandra.",
      "source": 1
    },
    {
      "fact": "The light is designed to sit on rimless tanks with glass thinner than 10 mm.",
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "fact": "The WRGB spectrum is said to suit tropical fish and plants.",
      "source": 5
    },
    {
      "fact": "The shop says the WRGB mix makes plants, fish and shrimp look more vivid without tinting the water.",
      "source": 2
    }
  ],
  "usage": [
    {
      "fact": "Adjustable legs or supports let the light fit tanks of different widths.",
      "source": 4
    },
    {
      "fact": "The dimmer comes in the box but is a separate inline part, not built into the light. The maker advises using only an original Twinstar dimmer.",
      "source": 5
    },
    {
      "fact": "The B II light has no timer of its own, so support suggests plugging it into a timer socket.",
      "source": 5
    },
    {
      "fact": "On the 30B III, the bundled dimmer has 6, 8 and 10 hour timer settings and a 10-minute sunrise/sunset ramp.",
      "source": 4
    },
    {
      "fact": "The light brightens gradually when switched on so fish are not startled. This still works when it runs on a socket timer.",
      "source": 2
    },
    {
      "fact": "The shop says the output comes tuned from the factory, so no app or adjustment is needed.",
      "source": 1
    },
    {
      "fact": "For online orders, the shop suggests filming the unboxing in case you need to make a claim.",
      "source": 1
    }
  ],
  "issues": [
    {
      "fact": "Specs differ between versions. The earlier 30B is listed at 9 W and about 679 lm, while the 2025 30B III is 11 W and 820 lm. Check which version a shop is selling.",
      "source": 3
    },
    {
      "fact": "The 2025 redesign is said to be brighter, have a better-balanced spectrum and be better built, but no figures are given for these claims.",
      "source": 3
    },
    {
      "fact": "Vietnamese shops often don't say whether they sell version II or III, and warranties range from 3 months to 12 months.",
      "source": 1
    },
    {
      "fact": "A UK retailer's spec table lists 0–25 W and 0–32 cm, which conflicts with its own 11 W and 36 cm figures.",
      "source": 4
    },
    {
      "fact": "A forum user found the Twinstar dimmer simple to use, but noted it has no display, timer presets are chosen with a button, and the older unit had no sunset function.",
      "source": 10
    },
    {
      "fact": "I found no forum reports of noise, failures or durability problems for the 30B.",
      "source": 10
    }
  ],
